    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Question\n\ncsharpls-extended-lsp.nvim is a plugin which overrides `textDocument/definition` & `textDocument/typeDefinition` handlers on the `csharp_ls` lsp; when setting it up, in C# files, `min.pick` isn't used for picking on definitions anymore.\r\nthe setup:\r\n\r\n```\r\nlspconfig['csharp_ls'].setup({\r\n    handlers = {\r\n        [\"textDocument/definition\"] = cslsex.handler,\r\n        [\"textDocument/typeDefinition\"] = cslsex.handler,\r\n    },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nis there an easy way to make this work with `mini.pick`?!",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.pick</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">csharpls-extended-lsp.nvim is a plugin which overrides <code class=\"notranslate\">textDocument/definition</code> &amp; <code class=\"notranslate\">textDocument/typeDefinition</code> handlers on the <code class=\"notranslate\">csharp_ls</code> lsp; when setting it up, in C# files, <code class=\"notranslate\">min.pick</code> isn't used for picking on definitions anymore.<br>\nthe setup:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"lspconfig['csharp_ls'].setup({\n    handlers = {\n        [&quot;textDocument/definition&quot;] = cslsex.handler,\n        [&quot;textDocument/typeDefinition&quot;] = cslsex.handler,\n    },\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">lspconfig['csharp_ls'].setup({\n    handlers = {\n        [\"textDocument/definition\"] = cslsex.handler,\n        [\"textDocument/typeDefinition\"] = cslsex.handler,\n    },\n})\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">is there an easy way to make this work with <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.pick</code>?!</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.pick\nQuestion\ncsharpls-extended-lsp.nvim is a plugin which overrides textDocument/definition & textDocument/typeDefinition handlers on the csharp_ls lsp; when setting it up, in C# files, min.pick isn't used for picking on definitions anymore.\nthe setup:\nlspconfig['csharp_ls'].setup({\n    handlers = {\n        [\"textDocument/definition\"] = cslsex.handler,\n        [\"textDocument/typeDefinition\"] = cslsex.handler,\n    },\n})\n\nis there an easy way to make this work with mini.pick?!",
