                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Congrats on going the whole way!\r\n\r\nOne minor issue: I'd suggest not using `::continue::`, as that is (strictly speaking) not a feature of Lua 5.1. Plugins and user configs should target its syntax (see `:h lua-compat`). It looks pretty straightforward to refactor it into two separate functions and use `return fetched` instead of `goto continue` and `::continue::`.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Congrats on going the whole way!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">One minor issue: I'd suggest not using <code class=\"notranslate\">::continue::</code>, as that is (strictly speaking) not a feature of Lua 5.1. Plugins and user configs should target its syntax (see <code class=\"notranslate\">:h lua-compat</code>). It looks pretty straightforward to refactor it into two separate functions and use <code class=\"notranslate\">return fetched</code> instead of <code class=\"notranslate\">goto continue</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">::continue::</code>.</p>",
